issues.body:
So when using the advancement packs [blaze and caves](https://modrinth.com/datapack/blazeandcaves-advancements-pack) and the addon [enhanced discoveries](https://modrinth.com/datapack/bacap-enhanced-discoveries), I noticed one of the advancements wasn't working, while it was in my creative world. I have lithium on my client so it seems to be a server thing.

The issue is that when I look at a spyglass item on the ground I am supposed to get the advancement "The Cult of the Spyglass" from the enhanced discoveries addon. In a creative singleplayer world or a server without lithium it works, but on a server with lithium it doesn't.

### Version Information

`lithium-fabric-0.24.2+mc26.1.2.jar`

### Expected Behavior

To unlock the achievement.

<img width="553" height="75" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/40c8bfb1-800c-4fd4-ba39-46637dfb1700" />

### Actual Behavior

Nothing happens.

### Reproduction Steps

1. Drop a spyglass item
2. Look at it through a spyglass

### Other Information

The advancement definition:
```
{
  "display": {
    "icon": {
      "id": "minecraft:spyglass",
      "components": {
        "minecraft:enchantment_glint_override": true
      }
    },
    "title": {
      "translate": "The Cult of the Spyglass"
    },
    "description": {
      "translate": "Look at a spyglass through the spyglass",
      "color": "#75E1FF"
    },
    "frame": "goal",
    "announce_to_chat": true
  },
  "parent": "bacaped:adventure/eye_contact_master",
  "criteria": {
    "look_to_spyglass": {
      "trigger": "minecraft:using_item",
      "conditions": {
        "player": {
          "type_specific": {
            "type": "minecraft:player",
            "looking_at": {
              "type": "minecraft:item",
              "nbt": "{Item: {id: \"minecraft:spyglass\"}}"
            }
          }
        },
        "item": {
          "items": "minecraft:spyglass"
        }
      }
    }
  },
  "rewards": {
    "function": "bacaped_rewards:adventure/the_cult_of_the_spyglass"
  }
}
```

**Is your feature request related to a problem? Please describe.**
<details><summary>As of 1.21.8 the code of <code>EntityNavigation#shouldJumpToNextNode</code> looks like this:</summary>

```java
private boolean shouldJumpToNextNode(Vec3d currentPos) {
	if (this.currentPath.getCurrentNodeIndex() + 1 >= this.currentPath.getLength()) {
		return false;
	} else {
		Vec3d vec3d = Vec3d.ofBottomCenter(this.currentPath.getCurrentNodePos());
		if (!currentPos.isInRange(vec3d, 2.0)) {
			return false;
		} else if (this.canPathDirectlyThrough(currentPos, this.currentPath.getNodePosition(this.entity))) {
			return true;
		} else {
			Vec3d vec3d2 = Vec3d.ofBottomCenter(this.currentPath.getNodePos(this.currentPath.getCurrentNodeIndex() + 1));
			Vec3d vec3d3 = vec3d.subtract(currentPos);
			Vec3d vec3d4 = vec3d2.subtract(currentPos);
			double d = vec3d3.lengthSquared();
			double e = vec3d4.lengthSquared();
			boolean bl = e < d;
			boolean bl2 = d < 0.5;
			if (!bl && !bl2) {
				return false;
			} else {
				Vec3d vec3d5 = vec3d3.normalize();
				Vec3d vec3d6 = vec3d4.normalize();
				return vec3d6.dotProduct(vec3d5) < 0.0;
			}
		}
	}
}
```

</details>

**Describe the solution you'd like**
This code may be optimized:
```java
Vec3d vec3d2 = Vec3d.ofBottomCenter(this.currentPath.getNodePos(this.currentPath.getCurrentNodeIndex() + 1));
Vec3d vec3d3 = vec3d.subtract(currentPos);
Vec3d vec3d4 = vec3d2.subtract(currentPos);
double d = vec3d3.lengthSquared();
double e = vec3d4.lengthSquared();
boolean bl = e < d;
boolean bl2 = d < 0.5;
if (!bl && !bl2) {
	return false;
}
```
to

```java
Vec3d vec3d3 = vec3d.subtract(currentPos);
double d = vec3d3.lengthSquared();
if (d < 0.5) {
	return false;
}
Vec3d vec3d2 = Vec3d.ofBottomCenter(this.currentPath.getNodePos(this.currentPath.getCurrentNodeIndex() + 1));
Vec3d vec3d4 = vec3d2.subtract(currentPos);
double e = vec3d4.lengthSquared();
if (e < d) {
	return false;
}
```

This _may_ result in less calculations in certain situations.

However I'm not sure if the optimization is worth it. This should be checked before implementing.

**Describe alternatives you've considered**
Doing nothing because it might be not not worth it.

**Additional context**
I discovered this while backporting changes related to rabbits into versions before 1.19.
* This specific code was introduced by the Mojang in 1.19 to address a problem where the path node was incorrectly advanced by 1
* It looks like it's related to small entities like rabbits or axolotls (introduced in 1.19)


_Note: Used mappings for code examples: Yarn 1.21.8+build.1_

